# The test dialect: @term/seed/code/test's mint and view files (ansi.tree, tint.tree). A file mixes ordinary Term
# statements with the dialect's own heads, so the grammar mines the definitions (`mint`, `tree`, `view` by name)
# and passes every other statement over with `mine node`. Read by the executor (compile/mill-run.ts), never by
# the ordinary compile path — the decision of mill-self-hosting's open question, settled 2026-08-29.

mine test
  mine list
    mine any
      mine form, like test-mint
        site mint
      mine form, like test-tree
        site tree
      mine form, like test-view
        site view
      mine node

mine test-mint
  mine term, term mint
    mine term
      site name
    mine list
      mine node

mine test-tree
  mine term, term tree
    mine term
      site name
    mine list
      mine node

mine test-view
  mine term, term view
    mine term
      site name
    mine list
      mine node
